-- title:
--   Existence of an even rigidified pair with prescribed Ω̂-image
-- statement:
--   Throughout, the following data and hypotheses are in force.
--
--   *Arithmetic data.* Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \neq r$, and a non-zero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   *The base ring.* A characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal O$ with an irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, whose residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has cardinality $r$ and for which $(r) = (\pi)$; $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   *The unramified cover.* A characteristic-zero domain $\mathrm{Onr}$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $\mathrm{Onr}$ is complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $\mathrm{Onr}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathrm{Onr}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) is given together with `hvdet`, which says that $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ holds precisely when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$; thus $\mathrm{vdet}$ is the $\pi$-adic valuation of the determinant.
--
--   *The indefinite quaternion algebra and its moduli.* Rationals $a, b$ with `hB`: $0 < a$ or $0 < b$, and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b]$ is a division algebra locally exactly at the places dividing $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$, with `hΛℤ` asserting $\mathbb Z \subseteq \Lambda$. A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point assignment `pt` for fake elliptic curves (abelian surfaces over a base with $\Lambda$-action, level-$N$ structure and the trace condition) and `h𝒳`, the statement that $(\mathcal X, f, \mathrm{pt})$ is a coarse moduli space in the sense of `IsCoarseModuli` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullback, bijectivity on algebraically closed fibres, and the universal property). An auxiliary level $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$, a fine moduli scheme $M$ over $\mathcal O$ for fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), and a group $G$ acting on $M$ by automorphisms $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ satisfying `hρ` (`IsLevelTwistAction`: the action is over the base, realises twisting of the level structure by $\chi(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). A morphism $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$, invariant under $\rho$ and compatible with the two point assignments (`hp`, `hρp`, `hp_pt`).
--
--   *Hecke correspondences.* For each prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$, a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$ for fake elliptic curves with an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup (`h𝒴`), together with two degeneracy maps $d_0 \ell, d_1 \ell : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$; `hd₀` says $d_0$ forgets the extra subgroup and `hd₁` says $d_1$ records the quotient by it along a level-$\ell$ isogeny. Two endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realising the Atkin–Lehner involutions at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   *The definite side.* Rationals $a_1, b_1$ with `hdef`: $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ is a division algebra locally exactly at the places dividing $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$, an idèle $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ with $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ Eichler of level $Nr$, an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$, and a prime $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ containing $r$. The group $\Gamma_t$ is characterised by `hΓt` as the group of units of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ integral for $R_1$ at every prime other than $v$. Families $s_\ell \in \mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]^{\times}$ and $s^f_\ell$ in the finite-adelic units satisfy `hs`: $s^f_\ell$ agrees with $s_\ell$ away from $r$, is trivial at $r$, the product of the diagonal idèle $\ell$ with $(s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $(\Lambda_1, \mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1)$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ at $\ell$ otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; and $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell \Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   *Special-fibre data.* A map $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathrm{Zp2}\,r \times \mathrm{Zp2}\,r$ satisfying `hcoord` (`IsOrderCoord`: additive, unital, multiplicative for the twisted multiplication involving the Frobenius of the Witt ring, injective, with dense image and the prescribed trace identity). Over the residue ring $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and `hA₀`, which says that $\theta_0$ identifies the formal group of $A_0$ with $X_0$ compatibly with the $\Lambda$-action through $\mathrm{coord}$. Families $e, e' : \Gamma_t \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with degrees $\mathrm{deg}$ and the hypotheses: `hE1` ($e\gamma, e'\gamma$ are an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\mathrm{deg}\,\gamma}$ preserving the level structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e\gamma$ up to powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (rational scalars $\gamma$ act through the $\Lambda$-action by that scalar, up to powers of $r$), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ is a scalar up to a power of $r$ then $\gamma$ is a scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring homomorphism of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a conjugating $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser whose image is $r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ is translated by $e\gamma$ through a label $\mathrm{lab}(\gamma) \in \Lambda$, multiplicative and compatible with scalars modulo $n$), and `hE4` (over any algebraically closed field receiving $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$, every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny of a fake elliptic curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e\gamma$, up to powers of $r$). An order $R_2 \subseteq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators in $R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`, `hR₂r`), a family $\hat e : R_2 \to \operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base, and the hypotheses `hE5a` (each $\hat e x$ is additive on points, commutes with the $\Lambda$-action and preserves the level structure), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unitality, multiplicativity, and integers acting through $\Lambda$), `hE5c` (composition with the star-conjugate gives multiplication by the reduced norm), `hE5d` (compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e$ on elements of the form $r^{k}\gamma$, up to powers of $r$), and `hE5e` (a single conjugating $g$ serves simultaneously for all $e\gamma$ and all $\hat e x$ in the formal-module description, with matrix images $r^{k}g\,\iota_0(\cdot)\,g^{-1}$).
--
--   *The Drinfeld side.* A ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathrm{Zp2}\,r \to \mathrm{Onr}$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`), a moduli package $\mathrm{MD}$ over $\mathrm{Onr}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and a family $\eta$ sending rigidified $\Phi$-data over $B$ to $\mathrm{MD}$-objects, with `hη` (three clauses: on admissible rigidified data $\eta$ identifies objects precisely when they are isomorphic; $\eta$ is natural in the base; and every $\mathrm{MD}$-object is, on a Zariski cover by localisations, of the form $\eta(t)$ for admissible $t$). An injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action into $M_2(K_0)$, with `hE₀` giving an integer $m$ such that $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ lies in the image and $r^{m}$ times the image lies in $M_2(\mathcal O)$. A family $e_D$ comparing $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}\,\mathcal O\,\mathrm{MD}$ with the product of the functor corepresented by $\mathrm{Onr}$ and Drinfeld's functor $\Omega$, subject to: `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity over every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent), `hfstD` (the first component of $e_D(x)$ is the structure leg $x.\psi$), `hGLD` (the action of $g$ in the sense of `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy` corresponds under $e_D$ to the $\mathrm{vdet}$-twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct`), `hPiD` ($\pi$-translation corresponds to twisting the leg by $\mathrm{Fr}$ and leaving the Deligne datum unchanged) and `hPiexD` (every object admits a $\pi$-translate). Finally a comparison $\kappa$ between $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ and $\mathrm{Onr}/(r)$ with `hκ`, and an isogeny $\beta_0$ from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   *Atkin–Lehner data on the special fibre.* A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$; a fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $\mathrm{Onr}/(\pi)$ with morphisms $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ over the base and an integer $k_w$, such that $(a_w, a_w')$ exhibits $A_{0w}$ as the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(b_w, b_w')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ preserving the level structure (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` provides, for any injective ring homomorphism of the centraliser of the $X_0$-action into $M_2(K_0)$, a single conjugating $g$ describing on formal coordinates all the $e\gamma$ as $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$ and the composite $a_w \!\cdot\! b_w$ as $r^{k_w'}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   *The comparison functor $\Xi$.* A family $\Xi$ sending, for each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and each $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$, a rigidified curve (a fake elliptic curve over $B$ together with a `Rigidification` relative to $A_0$: reductions modulo $\pi$, a pullback of $A_0$, and an $r$-power isogeny pair between them preserving levels) to a point of $\mathrm{ModuliPackage.G}$, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the leg of $\Xi$ is a $\mathrm{Fr}$-twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality in the base for pullbacks of rigidifications), `hΞiso` ($\Xi$ is constant on rigidified curves linked by an isomorphism compatible with the two legs up to powers of $r$) and `hΞdef` (over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, $\Xi$ is computed explicitly: there are $j \leq 1$ and an admissible rigidified datum $t$ with the prescribed formal module, transported from $\theta_0$ through $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$, such that $\Xi = \langle \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}\text{-twist of }\psi,\ \eta(t)\rangle$). An element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that $\Xi$ converts translation of a rigidification by $e\gamma$ into the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some $c \in \mathbb Z$ (`heqΓ`) and converts the Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ into the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ (`heqW`), both over connected Noetherian $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, the second under the additional assumption that $\bar r$ is invertible in $B$.
--
--   *Residue characteristic.* The hypothesis `h2`: $2$ is a unit in $\mathcal O$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses the following holds. Let $B$ be a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, let $\psi : \mathrm{Onr} \to B$ be an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, and let $P$ be a Deligne datum over $B$, i.e. an object of $(\mathrm{Omega}\ K_0\ \pi).\mathrm{obj}\,B$. Write $\psi^{\circ} := \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$ for the $\mathrm{Fr}$-twist of $\psi$ by minus the $\pi$-adic valuation of $\det g_0$. Then there exist a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ for $(\Lambda, N)$ and a rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ over $\psi^{\circ}$ such that:
--
--   (i) the leg of $\Xi\,B\,\psi^{\circ}\,\langle E, \varrho\rangle$ is $\psi^{\circ}$ itself (evenness);
--
--   (ii) `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct` holds for the element $g_0^{-1}$ between $e_D(\Xi\,B\,\psi^{\circ}\,\langle E, \varrho\rangle)$ and the pair $(\psi, P)$; that is, $\psi$ is the $\mathrm{Fr}$-twist of the first component of $e_D(\Xi\,B\,\psi^{\circ}\,\langle E, \varrho\rangle)$ by $-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0^{-1}) = \mathrm{vdet}(g_0)$, and for every full lattice $M$ in $K_0^{2}$ the line of $P$ at $M$ is the preimage, along the base-changed action of $g_0$, of the line of the second component of $e_D(\Xi\,B\,\psi^{\circ}\,\langle E, \varrho\rangle)$ at $g_0 \cdot M$.
--
--   This is the existence (surjectivity) half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld dictionary in the form used in this development: over a connected Noetherian base in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, every point of Drinfeld's formal upper half plane together with an unramified leg is realised by an even rigidified fake elliptic curve. It is stated in the frame of the formal-moduli comparison assembled from the coarse and fine moduli of fake elliptic curves, the Hecke and Atkin–Lehner correspondences, and the special formal module side, and is used by the accompanying uniqueness statement to produce the torsor identification of the two moduli problems.
